## Why This Is Asked
This evaluates expertise in deploying real-time ML systems within AWS for privacy-sensitive, multi-tenant environments requiring comprehensive monitoring, explainability, and rapid recovery capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- AWS PrivateLink and SageMaker endpoint architecture
- Private data lake integration with strict multi-tenant isolation
- Real-time drift detection and SHAP/IG explainability frameworks
- Provisioned concurrency and autoscaling for performance targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Explainer integration for inference transparency
function explainInference(model, input, featureNames) {
  const shapValues = model.predictSHAP(input);
  const igValues = model.predictIntegratedGradients(input);
  return {
    prediction: model.predict(input),
    explanations: {
      shap: shapValues,
      integratedGradients: igValues,
      featureNames: featureNames
    },
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    tenantId: extractTenantId(input)
  };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design multi-region, residency-compliant ML deployments combining real-time and batch workloads, governance, and automated rollback. Tests practical use of SageMaker Endpoint Variants, Model Registry, and drift tooling.

## Key Concepts

- Regional real-time endpoints with VPC isolation
- Per-region Feature Store governance
- Batch Transform for analytics
- Model Registry versioning
- Drift detection with Clarify
- Canary rollouts and automated rollback
- Cost controls and autoscaling

## Code Example

```javascript
// CDK deployment pattern for regional ML infrastructure
const modelPackage = new sagemaker.CfnModelPackage(this, 'ModelPackage', {
  modelPackageName: modelVersion.name,
  approvalStatus: 'Approved',
  sourceAccount: process.env.AWS_ACCOUNT_ID
